{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>וַיִּתְרֹצְצוּ הַבָּנִים, etc.</b> One needs to understand the verse's saying <b>וַיִּתְרֹצְצוּ</b>, and also its saying <b>לָמָּה זֶּה אָנֹכִי</b>. And Rashi explained: if the pain of pregnancy is this great, why do I long and pray for pregnancy — end of quote. And his explanation, may his memory be for blessing, the mind does not accept it, that the righteous woman would reject her pregnancy on account of the pain; also, how would her mind be set at rest by telling her, 'שְׁנֵי גוֹיִם,' etc., and through this her pain would not be removed. And our Sages, may their memory be for blessing, expounded many interpretations, but the plain sense of the verse was not known. However, the plain sense of the verse is that <b>וַיִּתְרֹצְצוּ</b> is an expression of crushing, meaning they were under extreme pressure as they kept thrusting against each other and would not be sustained in her womb, and this indicates that her pregnancy would not endure. <b>וַתֹּאמֶר אִם כֵּן לָמָּה זֶּה אָנֹכִי</b> — meaning, 'this' points back to the pregnancy: why am I pregnant — for nothing have I labored. <b>וַתֵּלֶךְ לִדְרֹשׁ אֶת ה׳</b> — meaning, to seek mercy for the endurance of her pregnancy and to know the matter surrounding their loss, for from heaven they would not perform a miracle for falsehood, that she would be remembered with something that does not endure. And she was never distressed over the pain of pregnancy, for the righteous endure great suffering in this world for the sake of eternal good."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:19.876122812Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}